<LayoutPage title="Foldster's Projects — About" description="Who we are">
  <h1>About Foldster's Projects.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A creator-experience consultancy run by Matt Giallourakis out of Fort Lauderdale, Florida.
  </p>

  <p>
    Foldster's Projects builds the digital + physical brand stack for streamers and content creators &mdash; overlays, interactive bots, custom tools, 3D-printed merch, branded apparel &mdash; as one cohesive package or à la carte.
  </p>

  <h2>The thesis.</h2>
  <p>
    Creators who want a consistent brand identity across digital and physical currently coordinate four or five different vendors: overlay designer, bot developer, 3D printer, print-on-demand vendor, social media manager. Each handoff loses brand cohesion. Foldster's Projects is one entity delivering "the stream looks like the merch looks like the bot's voice looks like the apparel."
  </p>

  <h2>How we work.</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Free tools as portfolio.</strong> Every tool on the site (Demowall, Demodrip, Demosky, palette tools, emotions.dev, Foldster Studio) is real, open source where it can be, and stays free forever. They are how we prove we can build.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Paid custom builds as revenue.</strong> When a creator wants the tools tailored to their brand &mdash; or wants the full digital + physical package &mdash; that's the work we charge for. Code shipped is code clients own. No DRM, no subscription lock-in, no recurring license fees.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Transparent pricing.</strong> Tiers are published on the <a href="/services/">services page</a>, not gatekept behind a "contact us for a quote." Rare in this space; deliberate differentiator.
  </p>

  <h2>The team.</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Matt</strong> &mdash; 15 years of code (TypeScript, Kotlin, Python, C/C++, GLSL) across mobile, web, and embedded hardware. Sr. Software Engineer at Ritz-Carlton Yacht Collection by day; consultancy by night and weekend. ME + MS EE background, generative art for fifteen years before that.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Dizzy</strong> &mdash; partner and the physical-side collaborator on Complete Package projects (merch fulfillment, packaging, brand). Currently pursuing an MS in Coastal & Marine Management.
  </p>

